        {
          "path": "_m/g/f/5/w/sconser-wp/sligachan-banner-bridge.jpg",
          "filename": "Sligachan banner Bridge.jpg",
          "caption": "Sligachan Bridge on the Isle of Skye. Immediately to the left of this bridge the only road from the south branches towards Portree and Dunvegan. On the far left one can catch a glimpse of Sligachan Hotel, on the far right one can see the slope of a Red Cuillin hill. Through the central arch one can spot a part of the new road bridge. As the weather was changing from sun to fog and back in short distances and moments on that day, one can see a few faint cloud bands in the sky.",
          "alt": "Sligachan Bridge on the Isle of Skye. Immediately to the left of this bridge the only road from the south branches towards Portree and Dunvegan. On the far left one can catch a glimpse of Sligachan Hotel, on the far right one can see the slope of a Red Cuillin hill. Through the central arch one can spot a part of the new road bridge. As the weather was changing from sun to fog and back in short distances and moments on that day, one can see a few faint cloud bands in the sky.",
